  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through Friday)\nIssued at 404 PM CDT SAT OCT 24 2026\n\nThis afternoon at the surface, a large area of high pressure is\npresent across much of the eastern half of Conus. In the upper levels,\nnortherly flow is present. Dry conditions will persist through the\nseven day forecast with warm days and cool nights. A surface low is\npresent over Central Canada today with an associated front extending\nout to the south of it into Minnesota and back into the Plains. \nUpper ridging will start out over the Central US and traverse into\nEastern Conus by the end of the weekend. We will remain in an \noverall rain free pattern with little available moisture for rain.\nWe may have enough moisture for some cloud cover for Monday \nthrough Wednesday with some minor perturbations in the upper flow.\nHowever, the lower levels will remain dry with no major frontal \nsystem set to move through the area through the forecast. \nTemperatures will remain fairly similar through the middle of the \nupcoming week with lows in the 40s to the lower 50s and highs \ngenerally in the 70s across Central Alabama. Toward the end of the\nweek, our low level flow begins to turn more east- southeast. This\nwill allow for a little moderating of our airmass with more 50s \nand some lower 80s mingling in with the respective lows and highs \nby Thursday into next weekend.\n\n08",
